{
  "id": "ep057",
  "duration": 60.072,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.822,
      "text": "A hundred million dollar Mars orbiter vanished from a simple math mix-up.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Mars Climate Orbiter 2.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL/Corby Waste",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mars_Climate_Orbiter_2.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 1.7,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 1.7,
          "end": 4.833,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.822,
      "end": 10.167,
      "text": "Most people assume it was a sudden rocket failure, but the truth hid in software.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Delta II launches with Mars Climate Orbiter.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Delta_II_launches_with_Mars_Climate_Orbiter.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.833,
          "end": 10.167,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 10.167,
      "end": 15.787,
      "text": "Lockheed Martin built the spacecraft to calculate thrusters using pound-force seconds.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Preparing Juno for WAVES installation.jpg",
        "credit": "Photo credit: NASA/Frankie Martin",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Preparing_Juno_for_WAVES_installation.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 10.167,
          "end": 13.0,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 13.0,
          "end": 15.8,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 15.787,
      "end": 22.582,
      "text": "Meanwhile, NASA navigation software expected metric newton-seconds for those exact thrusters.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Mission Operations Control Room during Apollo 9.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mission_Operations_Control_Room_during_Apollo_9.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 15.8,
          "end": 19.6,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 19.6,
          "end": 22.567,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 22.582,
      "end": 31.307,
      "text": "Because one pound-force equals about 4.45 newtons, the system treated force as twenty-two percent of its actual value.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 22.567,
          "end": 31.3,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 31.307,
      "end": 36.902,
      "text": "Those tiny uncorrected errors accumulated over a nine-month journey across space.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Mars - Over Gale Crater (45991611011).jpg",
        "credit": "Kevin M. Gill",
        "license": "CC BY 2.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mars_-_Over_Gale_Crater_(45991611011).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 31.3,
          "end": 36.9,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 36.902,
      "end": 44.427,
      "text": "On September twenty-third, nineteen ninety-nine, the probe plunged to a lethal altitude of just thirty-five miles.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "PIA07500.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PIA07500.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 36.9,
          "end": 40.667,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 40.667,
          "end": 44.433,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 44.427,
      "end": 51.872,
      "text": "Navigators spotted discrepancies earlier, but managers dismissed their warnings because proper paperwork was missing.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Bill Tindall (left) and Gene Kranz in Mission Control during Apollo 11.png",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bill_Tindall_(left)_and_Gene_Kranz_in_Mission_Control_during_Apollo_11.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 44.433,
          "end": 51.867,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 51.872,
      "end": 59.722,
      "text": "That fatal refusal to file correct forms is why a hundred million dollar Mars orbiter vanished from a simple math mix-up.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Mars Climate Orbiter 2.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL/Corby Waste",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mars_Climate_Orbiter_2.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 51.867,
          "end": 60.067,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
